(
 '# GitHub'
 ''
 'The package `GitHubAPIv3` offers an API in order to retrieve data from GitHub, and trigger actions in case the user has been properly authorized.'
 ''
 'The `]GitHub.*` user commands are an interface to `GitHubAPIv3` that allows a user to take advantage of some of the API functions.'
 ''
 'These user commands are available:'
 ''
 '* `ListRepos` lists the repositories of an owner'
 '* `ListIssues` lists the open issues of a repository'
 '* `ReportAllIssues` reports the issues over all repositories of an owner'
 '* `GoToGitHub` opens a repository on GitHub in the default browser'
 ''
 'More user commands will be added according to demand.'
 ''
 'Every one of them is also available as a function: the package exposes an API, so all of them can be'
 'executed under program control. See the ReadMe file for details.'
 ''
 'Note that all user commands require the specification of an _owner_. The owner can be saved permanently by passing the `-permanent` flag.'
 ''
 'Once saved, the user does not need to specify the owner, unless it changes.  '
)
